^"stream"{
 >>[2026-10-12 10:59] verify — Patches 4 (dfafb7ef), 5B and 6/6A/6B are in, and the review log (b87c59f5) sets the image rule. public/images/README.md is still 13 lines and names neither the renders.studies registry in .spw/assets.spw nor the staging rules in asset-management.spw, so Patch 1B is open and needs no one's call. Promoting a mark waits on the creator's pick, and Patches 2.5 and 7 still have no owner.
 >>[2026-11-05 23:05] cache — the creator: more of their own art linking pages instead of Midjourney art in random places; the images often do not feel cohesive thematically; more of their art, more immediately, from more pages. Census in PLAN.md: 23 of 214 route pages open on hand-made art and 138 carry no image; of 1,816 link images, renders outside the asset catalog are 9, and the families a folder does not settle (primes 150, illustrations 134, routes 92, home 52) are the open question #>wonder_midjourney_design_concepts_whose_hand. Four slices proposed: who made it, a sensor, links matched to their destination, more pages opening on the creator's art.
 >>[2026-11-05 23:55] land — first batch: twelve pages open on the creator's art in place of model renders, each piece matched to its page by its own lettering (topics, software, complexity, math, pedagogy, about, about/website, site design, architecture, craft, film storyboard, recipes); captions describe the piece and keep the old captions' links behind one Next:. The sidecars settled most of the provenance question: primes are scanned cutouts, illustrations are model renders (eight name Midjourney); routes/ and home/ have no sidecars and are taken as model renders until the creator says otherwise. A systems-layer rule now keeps every scan family whole: its own ratio, letterboxed when tall, never cropped to a frame's shape (systems/image-interaction.css). Statistics was held: Honk Bazongas ties to it only by its graph paper. Services, RPG Wednesday and Design wait: the first on the tuning seat, the second on whose art it is, the third on a look at the worktable scans.
 >>[2026-11-06 11:30] cite — the creator's material path for the cauldron: spells handwritten on washi tape with origami or pop-up work, scanned; Grok Imagine animating the scans; Midjourney interpreting the materials into a more imaginative frame. Each arrives through this plan's intake rule (one image, sidecar and registry, one placement); spellcraft-authoring holds the cauldron side.
